Data Privacy Vocabulary (DPV)
-----------------------------

This repository includes material copied from and derived from the Data
Privacy Vocabulary (DPV) 2.3, https://w3id.org/dpv/2.3, of the W3C Data Privacy
Vocabularies and Controls Community Group, whose files name their contributors
and the citation they ask for. Copyright (c) 2026 World Wide Web Consortium.
https://www.w3.org/copyright/software-license-2023/

This project is not endorsed by the Community Group or by W3C.

upstream/ holds the release's Turtle files, examples, two mapping folders'
files and LICENSE.md, unchanged, at the tag dpv-2.3, commit cbcd215. A DPV
vocabulary header names the W3C Document License
(https://www.w3.org/copyright/document-license-2023/), and the repository's
LICENSE.md names the W3C Software and Document License, reproduced below.

The changes this project made in what it derives from those files:

- src/dpv/data/ restates each vocabulary, concept scheme, term and example as
  a YAML record. It leaves out the statements that say how DPV's site publishes
  a file (prof:hasResource and the resource descriptors), skos:narrower and
  schema:domainIncludes and schema:rangeIncludes, which tests/test_coverage.py
  shows follow from what the records hold.
- src/dpv/data/dpv-2.3-examples.yaml also restates each example file's
  statements as records. An example file declares no prefixes, so this project
  supplies them, and a blank node takes a label of this project's. Three files
  that do not parse hold a note of the fault and no statements.
- src/dpv/schema/ gives each DPV property a slot and each kind of term a class,
  with DPV's own label and definition. dpv_core.yaml and the converter's tables
  add this project's own titles and descriptions.
- src/dpv/mappings/ restates DPV's ISO and ODRL mapping files as SSSOM.
- The source of a term's text is DPV. DPV's definitions may cite or follow the
  laws and standards they describe, and those keep their own terms. The location
  vocabulary's codes and addresses are as DPV publishes them, and this project
  read no ISO publication in making any of this.

